{"status":"fulfilled","value":{"name":"ops-01","output":"{
  "message_id": "logistics-ops-01",
  "speech": "My operational reading is that the reported increase in exceptions needs investigation, while we can make exception handoffs clearer this week. I am not treating training as the established cause. My private evidence is consequential: supervisors have no agreed overnight override owner (L-O1); each worker has only 15 minutes available this week, with no full-shift shutdown (L-O2); and a senior dispatcher can staff one two-hour exception clinic but cannot cover every shift (L-O3).\n\nI propose a bounded operational package: spend 2 units on workflow ownership, ask you to scope a 2-unit segmented audit, reserve 2 units for brief practice, and spend 1 unit consulting the learning scientist. That totals 7 of 10 units, leaving 3 unallocated pending our discussion. I would name an overnight override owner and handoff route, issue a short job aid, and verify that the owner is identified at each overnight handoff. Practice would stay within each worker's 15-minute limit; the clinic would be one scheduled session, with attendance and uncovered shifts recorded rather than assumed covered. I would withhold any independent-competence certification from this proposed release.\n\nAnalyst, what does your evidence establish about the denominators and where the reported increase occurred, and can you scope that audit within 2 units? I also request the scientist's advice on what the six-item check could support and how to fit useful practice and a changed-case check within our actual time and budget.",
